  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_lunacu",
      "name": {
        "en": "Lunacub's Badge",
        "zh": "子月证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_lunacu",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Lunacub has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for defeating enemies from long range.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Sniper Operator during field operations to exercise Deadeye responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员子月擅长在远距离击溃敌人\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为狙击干员，行使神射手职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_lunacu",
      "name": {
        "en": "'A Hidey-Hole That Moves'",
        "zh": "“移动的窝”",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "Y",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_lunacu",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operators occasionally see Lunacub's tent out on the Rhodes Island deck.\nIt's not in line with code, of course. Lunacub has her own dormitory (even if she's not often indoors), and camping on the deck violates Rhodes Island safety and firefighting regulations, but still she assiduously avoids patrols, setting up her tent on the deck again and again, always somewhere where she can get a clear view of the sky.\nThe tent was built by Lunacub herself, although 'built' might not be the best word: it moreso resembles fabric pieced together into one, then propped up as best she can so the wasteland gales don't blow it down so easily. What's noteworthy is where the fabric originates—\nFollowing Lunacub's eleventh time this quarter attempting to sneak into the warehouse and tripping the security system, Rhodes Island HR had a thorough conversation with her, and found in her possession several unregistered Rhodes Island uniforms (parts of which were shorn off and sewn into her tent). Lunacub's manners were impeccable during the conversation, expressing that she was 'just passing by,' and that 'on the outside, you can take stuff if nobody's watching it.' HR rectified the lapse in Lunacub's understanding, reiterated Rhodes Island discipline, as well as inquired as to where certain other parts of the tent fabric had come from.\n'The grey cloth? I found it in the forest. It was hanging on a tree. I pulled it down.'\n'This one's really warm, so it's really useful when it snows. I found it too, buried in a hole. Agnese told me about it.'\n'This one's amazing, it stops water! Someone gave it to me. I know what that look is—really, he did! I gave him directions, and he said it was payment!'\n'No, this isn't... um, these clothes are okay because they went through proceedings? You said something about application proceedings—how do you do that?'\n'This pelt is my friend's. I miss her a lot.'\nLunacub declined HR's proposal to provide her with a standard-issue Rhodes Island tent.",
        "zh": "干员们偶尔能在罗德岛的甲板上看到子月的帐篷。\n这当然不合规矩，子月有自己的宿舍（虽然她不常在里面），在甲板上居住也违反了罗德岛的安全与消防相关条例，但她仍然孜孜不倦地躲过巡查人员，一次次把自己的小帐篷架设在甲板上，架设在能一眼看到天空的地方。\n这顶帐篷是子月亲手制作的，“制作”这个词似乎不太恰当，她更像是把一堆布料随便拼在了一起。然后尽量把它牢靠地支撑起来，不至于被荒野的大风轻易吹垮。不过这些布料的来源——\n在子月本季度第十一次试图潜入仓库并触发安保系统后，罗德岛人事部门与她进行了一次深入的谈话，并从她那里查获了数件未经登记的罗德岛制服（部分已被剪开并缝制在了她的帐篷上）。在谈话中，子月态度良好，表示自己“只是偶然路过”，“在外面，没人看着的东西就是可以随便捡的”。人事部门纠正了子月的认知偏差，向该干员重申了罗德岛的纪律，并且与她交流了帐篷上部分其他布料的来源。\n“那块灰色的布？我在森林里捡到的。挂在树上，我就拿下来了。”\n“这块布很暖和，下雪的时候很有用，也是捡到的，埋在一个坑里，阿涅塞告诉我的。”\n“这个可厉害了，能防水！是一个人给我的。你那是什么表情，真的是他给我的！我帮他们指了下路，他说这是报酬！”\n“不，这个不是……呃，这件衣服有手续所以没关系？你刚才说的什么申请手续是怎么办的来着？”\n“这块毛皮是我朋友的。我很想她。”\n子月拒绝了人事部门向她配发罗德岛制式外勤帐篷的提议。",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ],
